k" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Owl&nbsp;2</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;And&nbsp;this&nbsp;one&nbsp;is&nbsp;my&nbsp;former&nbsp;profile&nbsp;pic</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"><img src="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/barredowl-s-kick-ass-art-page/pic.png" alt="pic.png" class="image" /></div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Owl&nbsp;3&nbsp;(featuring&nbsp;grumpy&nbsp;researcher)</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;In&nbsp;which&nbsp;an&nbsp;understaffed&nbsp;Foundation&nbsp;hires&nbsp;a&nbsp;plain-ass&nbsp;owl&nbsp;to&nbsp;do&nbsp;their&nbsp;dirty&nbsp;work</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"><img src="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/barredowl-s-kick-ass-art-page/owl.png" width="450px" alt="owl.png" class="image" /></div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Owls&nbsp;4&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;5</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;And&nbsp;this&nbsp;one&nbsp;is&nbsp;my&nbsp;current&nbsp;profile&nbsp;pic&nbsp;and&nbsp;its&nbsp;variant</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"><img src="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/barredowl-s-kick-ass-art-page/barredowl7.png" width="450px" alt="barredowl7.png" class="image" /><img src="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/barredowl-s-kick-ass-art-page/barredowl6.png" width="450px" alt="barredowl6.png" class="image" /></div> </div> </div> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-2" style="display:none"> <h2><span>About the Artist</span></h2> <div class="scp-image-block block-center" style="width:600px;"><img src="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/barredowl-s-kick-ass-art-page/headerNEW.png" style="width:600px;" alt="headerNEW.png" class="image" /> <div class="scp-image-caption" style="width:600px;"> <p>Pictured: me</p> </div> </div> <p>Hey all, I'm <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/barredowl" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6001754&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606790725" alt="barredowl" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6001754)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/barredowl" >barredowl</a></span>, a somewhat ambitious artist and turtleneck sweater enthusiast. As of now, I mostly draw via a little program by the name of Photopea. It's trash, sure, but it's <em>my</em> trash, you know?</p> <h2><span>The Process</span></h2> <h4><span>Pixel Art</span></h4> <p>So usually, when I'm thinking of drawing an SCP, I usually tend towards a situation which I can easily display. For example, maybe the interview log in <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3980">SCP-3980</a>, or the gramophone from <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3939">SCP-3939</a>. If it's just a simple humanoid, I usually just draw their face. I occasionally just draw a character from the SCP, such as the Masquerade figure from <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4430">SCP-4430</a>.</p> <p>After I've fully convinced myself that drawing that part of the SCP is going to be fun, I head over to a <a href="https://lospec.com/palette-list">palette list</a> and select something that catches my eye (usually a four-color palette, since that's the easiest to handle in Paint 3D). I download it via a .txt file and head over to Paint 3D to select the individual colors using a hex code.</p> <p>Then, I shift the canvas to an appropriate size. If it's smaller (i.e, a humanoid picture) I usually choose a 30x30 canvas. If it's larger (i.e a situation I want to illustrate) I shoot for a 60x60. Then, I get to drawing, expand the canvas to 300x300 once it's finished, and publish it here!</p> <h4><span>Drawings</span></h4> <p>I usually just draw SCPs that I like, to be honest. Nothing really special. The only real fun tidbit I have to share about the process is that most of my drawings, if colored, are sampled from a <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giorgio_de_Chirico">Giorgio de Chirico</a> painting. You can find the painting sampled from <a href="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1b/De_Chirico%27s_Love_Song.jpg">here</a>!</p> <h2><span>Contact Information</span></h2> <p>If you want to reach out to me, whether it be commissions, words of praise, or your deepest, darkest confessions, here are some of the sites you can contact me from!</p> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>Platform</th> <th>Username</th> </tr> <tr> <td>Wikidot</td> <td><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/barredowl">barredowl</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>IRC</td> <td>barredowl</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Reddit</td> <td><a href="https://www.reddit.com/user/barredowl_">barredowl_</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Instagram</td> <td><a href="https://www.instagram.com/barredowl_/">barredowl_</a></td> </tr> </table> <p>For future reference, I typically don't charge money for commissions, but if you want me to draw something, that article better be damn good or draw-able.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="licensebox22"> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">‡&nbsp;Licensing&nbsp;/&nbsp;Citation</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">‡&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;Licensing&nbsp;/&nbsp;Citation</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p>Cite this page as:</p> <p>For more information, see <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/licensing-guide">Licensing Guide</a>.<br /> <strong>Licensing Disclosures</strong></p> <div class="content-separator" style="display: none:"></div> <blockquote> <p><strong>Filename:</strong> All images<br /> <strong>Author:</strong> <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/barredowl" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6001754&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606790725" alt="barredowl" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6001754)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/barredowl" >barredowl</a></span><br /> <strong>License:</strong> CC BY-SA 3.0<br /> <strong>Source Link:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/barredowl-s-kick-ass-art-page">SCP Foundation Wiki</a></p> </blockquote> <div class="content-separator" style="display: none:"></div> <div class="content-separator" style="display: none:"></div> <p>For more information about on-wiki content, visit the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/licensing-master-list">Licensing Master List</a>.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/barredowl" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6001754&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606790725" alt="barredowl" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6001754)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/barredowl" >barredowl</a></span></p> 
