d>MTF-Zeta-5</td> <td>Lazarus Abominables</td> <td><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/apas">Automated Passive Amnestization System Ver. 17.09</a></td> <td>Assembled to perform aerial bombardment runs to subdue hazardous anomalies.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Zeta-7</td> <td>Homestead</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2341">SCP-2341</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces#zeta-9">MTF-Zeta-9</a></td> <td>Mole Rats</td> <td>See <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces">this page</a> for information about this particular task force.</td> <td>Exploration of areas with non-Euclidean or otherwise unusual topography.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Zeta-10</td> <td>Time Travelers</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-694">SCP-694</a></td> <td>Guards macroscopic time loops (and perhaps other temporal anomalies), as well as reducing public awareness of said loops.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Zeta-16-01</td> <td>Newspaper's Boys</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2703">SCP-2703</a></td> <td>Before it was disbanded, Zeta-16-01 was tasked with locating and confiscating newspapers containing instances of SCP-2703.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Zeta-16-02</td> <td>Gearlist</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2703">SCP-2703</a></td> <td>Before it was disbanded, Zeta-16-02 was tasked with tracking and deleting instances of SCP-2703 found in advertisements websites.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Zeta-16-03</td> <td>Restraining Orders</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2703">SCP-2703</a></td> <td>MTF-Zeta-16-03 is tasked with erasing instances of SCP-2703 written on public restroom doors.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Zeta-17</td> <td>Beach Bullies</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-777">SCP-777</a></td> <td>Routine myth verification.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Zeta-29</td> <td>Mad Mountaineers</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1936">SCP-1936</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Zeta-29</td> <td>Dragon Slayers</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1154">SCP-1154</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Zeta-29</td> <td>[DATA MISSING]</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1980">SCP-1980</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Zeta-40</td> <td>Dead-end Cleaners</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2002">SCP-2002</a></td> <td>No description given, presumably deals with salvage and cleanup.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Zeta-1000</td> <td>[DATA MISSING]</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1000">SCP-1000</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Zeta-Zeta</td> <td>Stardusters</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4172">SCP-4172</a></td> <td>An intelligence gathering and infiltration Task Force, performing on-the-ground surveillance of anomalous individuals within guerrilla performance-art groups, subversive theatrical troupes, underground art studios, and other insular creative spaces resistant to infiltration.</td> </tr> </table> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">▷&nbsp;Show&nbsp;list&nbsp;for&nbsp;'Eta'</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">◁&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;list</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <td>MTF-Eta-1</td> <td>Birdbrains</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3095">SCP-3095</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Eta-2</td> <td>Buyer Beware</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1808">SCP-1808</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces#eta-4">MTF-Eta-4</a></td> <td>Begone Thoth</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/bird">Team Bird Hub</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/join-the-flock">Join the Flock</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/spc-507">SPC-507</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3570">EE-3570</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/the-sacred-djehuti">The Sacred Djehuti</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/avian-anthology-i">Avian Anthology I</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/avian-anthology-ii">Avian Anthology II</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4688">SCP-4688</a></td> <td>A unit of intelligent <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3095">SCP-3095</a>-affected seabirds. Eta-4 specializes in information collection and analysis, field research, complementary field support, and in extreme cases, airborne combat. The task force was ultimately charged with protecting humanity after the BE-Class &quot;Migration&quot; End-of-Consciousness Scenario.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces#eta-5">MTF-Eta-5</a></td> <td>Jäeger Bombers</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2764">SCP-2764</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/lte-2712-bosch">LTE-2712-Bosch</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/animalia">Animalia</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5514">SCP-5514</a></td> <td>A rapid-response unit specializing in the tracking, capturing, and containment of Large-Scale Aggressors (entities over 30m in height). Deploys from, and detains LSAs within Dimensional-Site-172.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Eta-6</td> <td>Awareness Filters</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1504">SCP-1504</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Eta-6</td> <td><span style="color: red">Presented</span> <span style="color: green">In</span> <span style="color: blue">Color</span></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5020">SCP-5020</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5599">SCP-5599</a></td> <td>Investigation of <a target="_blank" href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/arcadia-hub">GoI-078</a> (<span style="color: purple">Arcadia</span>) and